cubic (2020.04) focal; urgency=low

  * Fixed Bug #1855153. Cubic will prevent the user from proceeding past
    the Project page if the custom ISO directory is invalid.

  * Issues fixed in version 2020.04-8:

  * Fixed Bug #1876190, Cubic crashes with Failed to open file
    "pages/source_view.ui" error. Added pages/source_view.ui file.

  * Issues fixed in version 2020.04-7:

  * Updated dependencies and versions. Fixes Bug #1876127.
  - Added python3-pydbus and systemd-container.

  * Set the style for the source views on the Preseed and ISO Boot tabs:
  - The system mono spaced font from org.gnome.desktop.interface
  - The Tango style scheme for colored fonts
  - The ini language for context highlighting

  * Removed prepare_utilities module and moved functions to prepare_page.

  * Renamed modules:
  - directory_file_chooser => directory_chooser
  - filepath_file_chooser => iso_image_chooser
  - constructors => constructor
  - display => displayer
  - navigation => navigator
  - process_utilities => processor
  - terminal_utilities => console

  * Removed print statements.

  * Issues fixed in version 2020.04-6:

  * Removed icon theme related functions from display.py.

  * Changed the original iso mount point name from "original-iso" to
    "source-disk" consistent  with the naming convention used with the
    custom iso, "custom-disk".

  * Adjusted the window dimensions to fit on 1024x768 screens. The pages
    are 976 px wide to allow space for a 48 px wide vertical dock. Pages
    use an aspect ratio of 3:2 for better readability. As a result, page
    height is 650 px, leaving 118 px available for window's title bar
    and horizontal docks of varying heights.

  * Issues fixed in version 2020.04-5:

  * Added missing exception type, ModuleNotFoundError, to navigation.py.

  * Issues fixed in version 2020.04-4 and 2020.04-3:

  * Corrected two errors ("TypeError: Argument 0 does not allow None as
     a value") on the Prepare page.
  * Moved cubic icons to /usr/share/icons/hicolor/scalable/status.
    Removed /usr/share/icons/Adwaita/, since Cubic can access the icons
    from hicolor for both light and dark theme variants. This aligns
    with best practices, since it is not always guaranteed that the
    Adwaita will be installed.
  * On the Packages page, set both the package column and the version
    column to expand.

  * Issues fixed in version 2020.04-2 and 2020.04-1:

  * Updated Cubic to use standard symbolic icons, which are responsive
    to light and dark theme changes and automatically adapt to hybrid
    header bars.
  * Removed dark and light icons from the /usr/share/cubic directory.
  * Added symbolic status icons in the Adwaita theme for cubic ok, cubic
    error, cubic optional, cubic bullet, and cubic blank.
  * Stopped monitoring style changes and dynamically updating the icon
    search path for light and dark themes, since this is no longer
    necessary.
  * Removed the PayPal icon from the Donate button.
  * Set the NEW_CUBIC_VERSION to '2020.04', so all projects created with
    a Cubic release prior to April 2020 will be migrated.
  * Corrected the Terminal Control Escape Sequence, used to reset the
    cursor position, to not print corrupted characters in Ubuntu 18.04.
  * Corrected an issue in Ubuntu 18.04 where the header bar title
    overlapped the tabs on the Options page.

 -- PJ Singh <psingh.cubic@gmail.com>  Thu, 30 Apr 2020 20:04:22 -0400
